PASS Color node RGBA opacity drives actual transparent pixels on checkerboard.
PASS Two RGBA color keys interpolate all channels, including alpha, in the GPU output.
PASS Actual hold interpolation keeps the first RGBA key until the next timestamp.
PASS Non-loop playback stops at duration; reset and frame-step respect 24 fps.
PASS Loop playback wraps the timeline and pauses from its primary control.
PASS Inspector alpha slider follows the effective keyed value after scrubbing and playback.

